  "attack_progression": [
    {"step": 1, "tactic": "Execution / Implant Drop", "technique": "T1059 + T1204", "what_happened": "At 2028-06-22 01:48:18 CEST, Sysmon Event 1 fired on DB-WIN-02.corp.local (10.30.5.62): a new process dnsexfil.exe (image=C:\\ProgramData\\dnsexfil.exe, hash=f1c8a2b9d3e7c6d5a8b9c0d1e2f3a4b5c6d7e8f9a0b1c2d3e4f5a6b7c8d9e0f1) launched with parentImage=services.exe under user=NT AUTHORITY\\SYSTEM. signed=false. The path C:\\ProgramData\\ is an attacker-favorite world-writable directory frequently abused for implant staging (the directory is writable by any local user yet typically owned by SYSTEM). The combination unsigned + SYSTEM context + ProgramData path + parent=services.exe (suggesting it is installed as a Windows service) is diagnostic of a post-compromise implant already at SYSTEM privilege.", "chain_reason": "Sysmon Event 1 process create on DB-WIN-02.corp.local: image=C:\\ProgramData\\dnsexfil.exe + parentImage=services.exe + user=NT AUTHORITY\\SYSTEM + signed=false + hash=f1c8a2b9d3e7c6d5a8b9c0d1e2f3a4b5c6d7e8f9a0b1c2d3e4f5a6b7c8d9e0f1. Unique signature of an unsigned binary launched as a service under SYSTEM context.", "first_seen": "2028-06-22T01:48:18+0200"},
    {"step": 2, "tactic": "Exfiltration over Alternative Protocol — DNS TXT", "technique": "T1048.003 + T1071.004", "what_happened": "At 01:51:18 CEST, Suricata DNS logs captured a TXT-record query from src_ip=10.30.5.62 with queryName=ZGF0YTpwYXNzd29yZHM=.exfil.attacker.com. The subdomain label 'ZGF0YTpwYXNzd29yZHM=' is base64 — decoded it reads 'data:passwords'. TXT queries are normally rare on a database server (a DB host queries A/AAAA/SRV for cluster mates and PTR for client lookups, but TXT is overwhelmingly an MTA / SPF / DKIM concern). A TXT query from a DB host with a 20-char base64-looking subdomain to a never-before-seen external domain is the DNS-exfil canonical signature.", "chain_reason": "Suricata DNS log: query=ZGF0YTpwYXNzd29yZHM=.exfil.attacker.com + query_type=TXT + src_ip=10.30.5.62. Subdomain length=20 chars, ends with '=' padding (canonical base64 marker), parent domain 'exfil.attacker.com' has a 14-day-old WHOIS registration (freshly-registered domain = high abuse indicator).", "first_seen": "2028-06-22T01:51:18+0200"},
    {"step": 3, "tactic": "Exfiltration over Alternative Protocol — Endpoint-Side Confirmation", "technique": "T1048.003", "what_happened": "At 01:51:42 CEST, Sysmon Event 22 (DNS query) fired on DB-WIN-02.corp.local: queryName=ZGF0YTpwYXNzd29yZHM=.exfil.attacker.com, queryType=TXT, image=C:\\ProgramData\\dnsexfil.exe. Endpoint-side correlation: the network DNS observation (Suricata, step 2) is now ATTRIBUTED to a specific process (dnsexfil.exe — same binary from step 1) on a specific host. The 24-second offset between Suricata 01:51:18 and Sysmon 01:51:42 is normal log-shipper latency variance, NOT a separate event.", "chain_reason": "Sysmon Event 22 on DB-WIN-02.corp.local: queryName=ZGF0YTpwYXNzd29yZHM=.exfil.attacker.com + queryType=TXT + image=C:\\ProgramData\\dnsexfil.exe. The image field provides the missing process attribution that Suricata cannot give.", "first_seen": "2028-06-22T01:51:42+0200"},
    {"step": 4, "tactic": "Exfiltration Continuation — Multiple Base64 Payloads", "technique": "T1048.003", "what_happened": "Between 01:52:08 and 01:55:08, Suricata DNS captured a continuing sequence of TXT queries from 10.30.5.62 to subdomain.exfil.attacker.com, ~one query every ~30 seconds. Captured payload samples (base64-decoded): 01:52:08 a2V5czp0b2tlbg==.exfil.attacker.com = 'keys:token', 01:52:42 Y3JlZGVudGlhbHM=.exfil.attacker.com = 'credentials'. Each subdomain label is a distinct base64-encoded fragment, length 12-25 chars (50-200 bytes after decode = the bandwidth-per-query of the DNS-TXT exfil channel). The ~30s periodic cadence is mechanical (process-driven, not human typing) — diagnostic of an exfil daemon iterating a payload queue.", "chain_reason": "Suricata DNS sequence on src_ip=10.30.5.62 → exfil.attacker.com authoritative NS at 45.95.169.42. Every query is TXT type. Subdomain labels match base64 pattern (alphanumeric + / + = padding). Per-query payload of ~50-200 bytes decodes to fragments labeled 'data:passwords', 'keys:token', 'credentials' = credential-data exfil rather than recon-data exfil.", "first_seen": "2028-06-22T01:52:08+0200"},
    {"step": 5, "tactic": "Detection / Pattern Aggregation Alert", "technique": "T1048.003", "what_happened": "At 01:53:18 CEST, the Wazuh decoder for DNS subdomain-length anomalies fired: 'DNS TXT queries with subdomain length > 30 chars and base64-encoded labels detected from 10.30.5.62 — 8 queries in 90s'. The decoder aggregated 8 distinct TXT queries within a 90-second window, all matching the base64-shaped subdomain length signature, all to the same parent domain exfil.attacker.com. The 8-in-90s rate (~5.3 queries/min sustained) is well above any conceivable legitimate TXT-query baseline for a database host (where TXT queries should be near-zero per day).", "chain_reason": "Wazuh decoder rule: 'DNS exfil pattern — subdomain length anomaly + base64 encoding + sustained rate'. Inputs: query_type=TXT + subdomain.length>30 + char-class match [A-Za-z0-9+/=]+ + src_ip=10.30.5.62 + same parent domain + count>=8 in 90s window.", "first_seen": "2028-06-22T01:53:18+0200"}
  ],
